{"height": 13, "weight": 445, "base_experience": 173, "ev_yield": [{"stat": "special-attack", "value": 2}], "genus": "Spitfire Pokémon", "capture_rate": 45, "base_happiness": 70, "hatch_counter": 25, "growth_rate": "medium", "egg_groups": ["humanshape"], "gender_rate": 2, "names": [{"language": "ja-hrkt", "name": "ブーバー"}, {"language": "ja-roma", "name": "Boober"}, {"language": "ko", "name": "마그마"}, {"language": "zh-hant", "name": "鴨嘴火獸"}, {"language": "fr", "name": "Magmar"}, {"language": "de", "name": "Magmar"}, {"language": "es", "name": "Magmar"}, {"language": "it", "name": "Magmar"}, {"language": "ja", "name": "ブーバー"}, {"language": "zh-hans", "name": "鸭嘴火兽"}, {"language": "es-419", "name": "Magmar"}], "pokedex_entries": [{"versions": ["red", "blue"], "text": "Its body always burns with an orange glow that enables it to hide perfectly among flames."}, {"versions": ["yellow", "lets-go-pikachu", "lets-go-eevee"], "text": "Born in an active volcano. Its body is always cloaked in flames, so it looks like a big ball of fire."}, {"versions": ["gold"], "text": "It dislikes cold places, so it blows scorching flames to make the environment suit­ able for itself."}, {"versions": ["silver", "soulsilver"], "text": "The fiery surface of its body gives off a wavering, rippling glare that is similar to the sun."}, {"versions": ["crystal"], "text": "It moves more frequently in hot areas. It can heal itself by dipping its wound into lava."}, {"versions": ["ruby", "sapphire"], "text": "In battle, MAGMAR blows out intensely hot flames from all over its body to intimidate its opponent. This POKéMON’s fiery bursts create heat waves that ignite grass and trees in its surroundings."}, {"versions": ["emerald"], "text": "In battle, it blows out intense flames from all over its body to intimidate its foe. These fiery bursts create heat waves that ignite grass and trees in the area."}, {"versions": ["firered", "x"], "text": "Found near the mouth of a volcano. This fire-breather’s body temperature is nearly 2,200 degrees Fahrenheit."}, {"versions": ["leafgreen"], "text": "Its body always burns with an orange glow that enables it to hide perfectly amidst flames."}, {"versions": ["diamond", "pearl", "y"], "text": "Born in the spout of a volcano, its body is covered by flames that shimmer like the sun."}, {"versions": ["platinum", "black", "white"], "text": "When it breathes deeply, heat waves form around its body, making it hard to see clearly."}, {"versions": ["heartgold"], "text": "It dislikes cold places, so it blows scorching flames to make the environment suitable for itself."}, {"versions": ["black-2", "white-2"], "text": "The scorching fire exhaled by Magmar forms heat waves around its body, making it hard to see the Pokémon clearly."}, {"versions": ["omega-ruby", "alpha-sapphire"], "text": "In battle, Magmar blows out intensely hot flames from all over its body to intimidate its opponent. This Pokémon’s fiery bursts create heat waves that ignite grass and trees in its surroundings."}, {"versions": ["sun"], "text": "When it’s tired, it leaps into the mouth of a volcano and soaks its body in magma to ease its weariness. Its body burns at 2,192 degrees F."}, {"versions": ["moon"], "text": "When angered, it spouts brilliant fire from all over its body. It doesn’t calm down until its opponent has burned to ash."}, {"versions": ["ultra-sun"], "text": "Its entire body is burning. When it breathes, the temperature rises. When it sneezes, flames shoot out!"}, {"versions": ["ultra-moon"], "text": "The hotter the place, the better they feel. Magmar in Alola are said to be hardier than those in other areas."}, {"versions": ["sword"], "text": "Magmar dispatches its prey with fire. But it regrets this habit once it realizes that it has burned its intended prey to a charred crisp."}, {"versions": ["shield"], "text": "These Pokémon’s bodies are constantly burning. Magmar are feared as one of the causes behind fires."}, {"versions": ["legends-arceus"], "text": "